    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Quantities of one kind are said to be inversely proportional to quantities of another kind, if the ratio of any two of the first kind is equal to the inverse ratio of the corresponding two of the other kind."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 23,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 31.0, 368.952, 300.667, 410.237 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 7.42,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "If 6 men can do a piece of work in 4 days, then 8 men can do it in 3 days, or 6:8 equals the inverse ratio of 4:3, 7.e.5:4. Hence the number of men required to do some work, and the time necessary to do it, are inversely proportional."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 24,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 30.333, 338.285, 301.0, 362.952 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
